L properties are improved by low-temperature passes\",\"explanation\":\"As-rolled steel is steel whose strength and toughness are enhanced by rolling passes in the low-temperature range just above Ar3. Its grain structure is refined by rolling passes. This links process parameters directly to final mechanical properties without additional heat treatment. [Data: Entities (1175); Relationships (2512)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Temperature dichotomy governs rolling-pass effectiveness\",\"explanation\":\"The community's core technical insight is that the effect of ROLLING PASSES depends on temperature. High-temperature passes do not contribute to refinement of γ-grain structure. In contrast, passes in the low-temperature range just above Ar3 refine grain structure and enhance strength and toughness in as-rolled steel, especially Nb steels. This dichotomy connects the process entities and explains why controlled rolling schedules are designed around temperature windows. [Data: Entities (226, 5, 1175); Relationships (309, 2535, 2512)]\"}],\"rating\":6.5,\"rating_explanation\":\"The impact severity is rated 6.5 because the community describes high-importance industrial process parameters that directly control grain refinement, strength, and toughness in as-rolled and Nb steels, but no legal, security, or reputational risk data are present.\"}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "reasoning_content": "We need answer only JSON object per schema. Need write community report based on provided entities/relationships. Must adhere schema: title, summary, findings array of {summary, explanation}, rating number, rating_explanation. No markdown. Need ground with data refs. Need not make up. This is about metallurgy/controlled rolling. Community key entities: ROLLING PASSES, ROUGH-HOLD-FINISH SCHEDULE, GRAIN STRUCTURE, NB STEELS, RAPID-RECRYSTALLIZATION REGION, AS-ROLLED STEEL, ROUGHER. Relationships listed. Ne